# deploy-t12/fleet.env.example — the TEMPLATE of fleet.env (fleet.env itself is untracked: `*.env` is
# in .gitignore). Copy it once on the Mac:  cp fleet.env.example fleet.env  — then fill it from the
# release build (PLAN.md §4). Every install-*.sh, build-release-5104.sh, distribute-from-mac.sh,
# check-fleet.sh and the seeder scripts source fleet.env; the drill kit reads its FORBIDDEN_GENESIS and
# DRILL_GENESES (../t12-drill-kit/lib.sh).
#
# Nothing below is a secret: no key, no password, no DB URI. Keys stay in KEY_DIR on each host and the
# kit only `test -f`s them.

# ---- the release (R-core+, ADR-0152 v3.1). __FILL_ME__ blocks `stage` / `switch` (lib.sh require_release) ----
# All of these are pinned from the SHIPPING commit only: the audit's deadline/P-1 (4-quater), A-held
# (feat/t12-aheld + the node half) and the Activation Pool merges each move the t12 params and may move
# the genesis. Values read from an earlier commit (docs/t12-rcore-launch-checklist.md §3 lists the
# provisional ones) are NOT to be pasted here.
REV=__FILL_ME__                  # 12-hex rev of the shipping commit (build-release-local.sh / build-release-5104.sh print it)
KASPAD_SHA256=__FILL_ME__        # sha256 of the fleet's x86_64 Linux kaspad: the release build that is SHIPPED — the Mac's
                                 # cross build (build-release-local.sh, preferred) or 5.104's (fallback); never a Mac-native build
MISAKA_SHA256=__FILL_ME__
PALW_CLASS_SHA256=__FILL_ME__
SEEDER_SHA256=KEEP               # KEEP = the 1174b965 seeders stay (SEEDERS.md §1); or the release's misaka-dnsseeder sha
# The release's own identity, read by an isolated probe of the release binary (build-release-local.sh's
# container probe of the cross-built kaspad, build-release-5104.sh's probe on 5.104, or
# probe-identity-local.sh on the Mac — the values are the same on any architecture: they are functions of
# the params and the genesis, not of the binary):
EXPECT_FP=__FILL_ME__            # "Consensus params fingerprint:" = getPalwNodeStatus.consensusParamsId (64 hex)
EXPECT_GENESIS=__FILL_ME__       # the genesis hash (128 hex) = a fresh node's pruning point
# The t12 premine txid the genesis bonds and fee floats sit on (`<PREMINE_TXID>:<card>`,
# `<PREMINE_TXID>:<41+card>`). The probe prints it from getPalwPanelSeats. 5e0d5f1b… at c8652a97 and at
# rcore/int-3 a0af3c92; it moves only if PALW_T12_PREMINE_SALT or the sentinel moves.
PREMINE_TXID=__FILL_ME__

# ---- geneses a public t12 node must never run (full hashes; require_release refuses EXPECT_GENESIS in
# either list, and switch refuses a node that announces a drill chain) ----
#   f6cc9576… the PRIVATE t12 (b791b460/5a559459; same card keys and premine — every private signature
#             and premine spend replays onto a chain that shares it) — handoff §6
#   fb1074b0… the live t12 being retired (2bd134ec, fp c746f07c)                              — handoff §6
#   a8cabac4… the 09-23 first regenesis                                                       — handoff §6
#   d73dbf44… t12 before the 100M community row (e93be0f2)                                     — handoff §6
#   1eaa6c0f… the FIRST pre-drill's salted chain (71c0399e, …/DRILL-PRE-e93be0f2)              — handoff §6 (drill 1)
#   32a665d6… the SECOND pre-drill's salted chain (005e5c5f, …/DRILL-PRE-c8652a97)             — handoff §6 (drill 2)
# a27f8f44… (c8652a97's public candidate, still PALW_T12_GENESIS at a0af3c92) is NOT listed: it is the
# shipping genesis unless R-core+'s genesis rows move it. If they do, add it here at the RE-PIN
# (docs/t12-rcore-launch-checklist.md §4 step 7): builds of c8652a97 exist that would run it.
FORBIDDEN_GENESIS="f6cc957686f7047dc9fe6c9619d8f487237574b0596573af9d337c8f1f1980151b26256967a9a81f7ae31a5a352e249dd5426c0ce9144f75eb26a3ca3a963a30
fb1074b0e7dd303158c0a3c79725a55700d731fd0bc654f739534341f566ae495f7aeae9ecbecc33bb997a6908d2adbf97dc5d3def6f5fad5d255e77e47469aa
a8cabac47b96fe30d9675ce08a355f62e6d57aac84865b0d6295c024c6d8ff61fb2d93943952e8da4c36ff87ea7f17f6c8de643fa7b02ecf7512892d590777dd
d73dbf44dbae3522c05de7aada567f9448221bc5c832393c9eb2996698e91aba2e638f0eea1f89bccbf72268750bb62deb1e958440136ca748727747f230fe18
1eaa6c0fb5e2223cf148ca64ef336a31f408be3f1d491c1edbf1f0da65f56b60806d1e0a264434bcca150288d951d41485fb1574abb79a273094e778b89d6d7c
32a665d622baba4cf97741da2fb68896463d668f794867d2ebd9db49a92634dc381b4250b3d734b251a2d161f3238820b4c3877807621e557fdf17cba994705f"
# The geneses of the post-launch drills (P2-12: `--palw-drill-genesis-salt=<salt>` moves the genesis per
# salt, so the list grows with each drill). Add one line per drill salt BEFORE that drill starts:
#   ./probe-identity-local.sh --drill-salt <64 hex>     prints `DRILL_GENESES+=" <128 hex>"`
# The salts themselves are not written here (a salt is the drill's, handed out of band — drill kit README).
DRILL_GENESES=""

# ---- fleet constants (unchanged by R-core+) ----
REL_ROOT=/root/t12-rel           # kit, incoming binaries, staged releases, switch state
INCOMING=$REL_ROOT/incoming
STATE_DIR=$REL_ROOT/state
APPDIR_PREFIX=/root/.t12r-b      # new appdirs /root/.t12r-b<N> — never an old chain's
KEY_DIR=/etc/misaka/t12          # t12-bond-<N>.key (the kit only test -f's it)
# The kit's copies of chain facts below (FEE_FLOAT_BASE, CLASS_8K, ART_8K_BYTES; lib.sh CLASS_2M_PREFIX;
# the explorer's LLM_CLASSES and PANEL_BOND_TX) are PINNED to the build by
# consensus/core/tests/t12_deploy_kit_constants.rs — re-run it at the re-pin (checklist §5); the switch
# gate and probe-identity-local.sh also compare them with what the running binary registers.
FEE_FLOAT_BASE=41                # card N's fee float is premine index 41+N (premine.rs MAIN_PREMINE_INDEX 40 + 1 + N)
# The heartbeat payout (PLAN.md §7/§10 Q10). The previous kit paid misakatest:qf6hf5v0…; that prefix is
# card 0's payout address — PALW_T12_GENESIS_BONDS[0].payout_payload, printed in full by
# t12_deploy_kit_constants (`LAYOUT card 0 … payout`) and `probe-identity-local.sh --layout`. The
# operator confirms it (or pastes another misakatest: address) before stage.
HB_ADDR=misakatest:qf6hf5v0nm2sj9ae8ryqswv3n78306fvhajahjesnsl0w68kdwq4g6pkf25cedz9leudhc739gqmz3z5we99vm6mfw497ymnpp82q7lggq7cte2n
# The 8k genesis row (graph-v7@8192, class ebf44d0a…) and its artifact — unchanged at a0af3c92
# (PALW_T12_GENESIS_QWEN25_A16_8K_ARTIFACT_ROOT is read from the committed sidecar, whose sha256 is
# MANIFEST_8K_SHA256):
CLASS_8K=ebf44d0aa09ff7d1310a7855ab4005c275cdce557e32c269b0f3a984ea80ca73ad1ea0c9b1c0539c8ae04abb5fe24399e67e05bb0895a3dee82253e772246d01
ART_8K=/root/palw-class/qwen25-1.5b-a16-8k.palwart
ART_8K_BYTES=1799359436
ART_8K_SHA256=b73600cfeef3f54fd6e9f6a831c504588aa3b20ea2506ae824799206201e8ac8
MANIFEST_8K_SHA256=c3cc66bc140a7fcbc949500f6ddcb6641a4d63f411c2f943e65750cd3875df4a
